The test failures were caused by the `SEPARATORS` regular expression not including whitespace characters. This meant that strings containing spaces were not being correctly split into words, leading to incorrect camelCasing.

I updated the `SEPARATORS` constant in `index.js` to include `\s`:

```javascript
// Old
const SEPARATORS = /[_.\-]+/;
// New
const SEPARATORS = /[\s_.\-]+/;
```

